  "body": "Stacked on #4073. This branch starts from `issue/1120-tool-inks` (25b220b34). Its own commit is d3e8dd705. Review that commit only. Merge #4073 first.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe fifth family of #1120: the verdict palettes.\n\n- The six colour-vision palettes (`Semantic::OFF`, `RED_GREEN`, `TRITAN`, `OFF_LIGHT_GROUND`, `RED_GREEN_LIGHT_GROUND`, `TRITAN_LIGHT_GROUND`) and the house text inks (`TextInks::HOUSE`) move out of `colorvision.rs` and `ground_ink.rs` into a new table file, `crates/ui/src/egui_app/theme/verdict.rs`.\n- No value changes. No name changes: the palettes stay associated consts of `Semantic` and `TextInks`, so no call site changes.\n- `colorvision.rs` keeps the types, the CIEDE2000 gate and the simulation maths (377 to 286 lines).\n- No theme-file key sets a verdict colour. #1120 says: \"The verdict colours (gouge, rest, move kinds) and their colour-vision maths stay ours and stay as they are - they move into the token table, they do not change value.\"\n- The colour-literal guard drops the `colorvision.rs` row (15) and gets a `keep:` row for `theme/verdict.rs` (15).\n- `docs/user-guide/themes.md`: a paragraph says that a theme does not set the colours that carry a meaning, and why.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/1120-verdict-inks.md`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\nIn `crates/ui/tests/theme_files/verdict_inks.rs`, a new module of the existing `theme_files` test binary (#3187: no new binary):\n\n- `each_colour_vision_palette_keeps_its_values_in_the_token_table`: each of the six palettes and `TextInks::HOUSE` equals the literals of the two files before the move, and `palette_for` gives the same set for each mode on each ground. The test passed on the code before the move, and passes after it.\n- `no_theme_key_sets_a_verdict_colour`: a theme file with `gouge`, `feed`, `warn` and other verdict names is refused with \"unknown token\".\n\nAlso: `colour_literals::no_colour_literal_outside_the_allowed_rows` and the colour-vision gate tests of the lib (`colorvision`, `ground`: 32 passed).\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThe first-part example with all toolpaths shown, cropped to the viewport, in the Off, Protan and Tritan modes. The images come from the off-screen renderer (`egui_kittest` with the headless wgpu device, as in `guide_images`), at 1200 x 760, then cropped. The images are on the images-only `pr-screenshots` branch of the fork.\n\nA pixel comparison of each full frame gives 0 different pixels. The Protan and Tritan frames differ from Off by about 9900 and 6900 pixels, so the shots show the remapped palettes. Before is 25b220b34; after is the head of #4208, which contains this commit and only a close-button change on top.\n\n| | Before (25b220b34) | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Off | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1120-verdict/before-vision-off.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1120-verdict/after-vision-off.png) |\n| Protan | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1120-verdict/before-vision-protan.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1120-verdict/after-vision-protan.png) |\n| Tritan | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1120-verdict/before-vision-tritan.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1120-verdict/after-vision-tritan.png) |\n\nThe images do not show a light viewport or the warning and error text inks. The test pins those values.\n\n## Gates\n\nOn d3e8dd705:\n\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): 10 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (2.8 min). It includes `ui suites: lib`, `ui suites: theme_example` and `ui suites: theme_files`.\n- `cargo clippy --no-deps --all-targets -p camcraft-ui -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Heavy lanes: the diff reaches none.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No check by hand in the GUI. The tests and the pixel comparison pin the values.\n\nChangelog: none (no behaviour change: the colour-vision palettes move into the token table with the same values).\n\nRefs #1120\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
